## Integration and Usage Example

```csharp
// Program.cs (example of how to integrate the modules)
public class Program
{
    public static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Setup DI container
        var services = new ServiceCollection();

        // Register services
        services.AddSingleton<IFileStorage, FileSystemStorage>();
        services.AddSingleton<IVirusScanner, ClamAVScanner>();
        services.AddSingleton<IInvertedIndex, InvertedIndex>();
        services.AddSingleton<ITokenizer, SimpleTokenizer>();
        services.AddSingleton<IRbacService, RbacService>();
        services.AddSingleton<IRoleStore, InMemoryRoleStore>();
        services.AddSingleton<IResourceStore, InMemoryResourceStore>();

        services.AddSingleton<ITextIndexingEngine>(provider =>
            new TextIndexingEngine(
                provider.GetRequiredService<IInvertedIndex>(),
                provider.GetRequiredService<ITokenizer>(),
                provider.GetRequiredService<ILogger<TextIndexingEngine>>()));

        services.AddSingleton<IFileUploadGateway>(provider =>
            new FileUploadGateway(
                provider.GetRequiredService<IVirusScanner>(),
                provider.GetRequiredService<IFileStorage>(),
                provider.GetRequiredService<ILogger<FileUploadGateway>>()));

        var serviceProvider = services.BuildServiceProvider();

        // Example usage
        var uploadGateway = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<IFileUploadGateway>();
        var rbacService = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<IRbacService>();
        var textIndexingEngine = serviceProvider.GetRequiredService<ITextIndexingEngine>();

        // 1. Upload a file
        using var fileStream = File.OpenRead("example.pdf");
        var uploadResult = await uploadGateway.ProcessUploadAsync(
            fileStream,
            "example.pdf",
            "application/pdf",
            CancellationToken.None);

        if (uploadResult.Success)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"File uploaded successfully. ID: {uploadResult.FileId}");

            // 2. Index the document
            await textIndexingEngine.IndexDocumentAsync(
                uploadResult.FileId,
                fileStream,
                CancellationToken.None);

            // 3. Check permissions
            var hasPermission = await rbacService.CheckPermissionAsync(
                "user123",
                uploadResult.FileId,
                "read",
                CancellationToken.None);

            Console.WriteLine($"User has read permission: {hasPermission}");

            // 4. Search documents
            var searchResults = await textIndexingEngine.SearchAsync(
                "important document",
                10,
                CancellationToken.None);

            foreach (var result in searchResults)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Document: {result.DocumentId}, Score: {result.Score}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Key Features Implemented

1. **File Upload Gateway**:
   - Handles multi-part MIME streams (can be extended with ASP.NET Core's multipart handling)
   - Virus scanning integration
   - File type validation
   - Asynchronous processing

2. **Full-Text Indexing Engine**:
   - Tokenization of text content
   - Inverted index implementation for efficient searching
   - Document update capabilities
   - Basic search functionality with scoring

3. **Role-Based Access Control**:
   - Permission checking for users on resources
   - Role assignment and management
   - Resource permission management
   - Flexible permission model

## Extensibility Points

1. **File Upload**:
   - Can integrate with cloud storage (Azure Blob, AWS S3)
   - Can add more sophisticated multipart handling
   - Can implement different virus scanning providers

2. **Text Indexing**:
   - Can integrate with dedicated search engines (Elasticsearch, Lucene)
   - Can add more sophisticated tokenization (stemming, stop word removal)
   - Can implement more advanced scoring algorithms

3. **RBAC**:
   - Can integrate with existing identity providers
   - Can implement more granular permission models
   - Can add audit logging for permission changes

This architecture provides a solid foundation for an enterprise document management system that can be further extended based on specific requirements.
